Omarchy is a beautiful, modern and opinionated Hyprland desktop originally
built for Arch Linux by DHH. This port brings the Omarchy experience to
FreeBSD, stripped to the essentials that make sense on a vanilla, minimal
install: the Hyprland compositor, the QuickShell top bar, a themed terminal,
Wayland utilities, fonts, themes, and a TTY-launch workflow.

The port pulls in the desktop dependencies and installs two helpers:

  omg              Launch the desktop from a TTY (sets up the FreeBSD Wayland
                   environment and execs Hyprland).
  omarchy-setup    Clone the Omarchy dotfiles into your home directory and
                   apply the FreeBSD path adaptations.

After installing, run `omarchy-setup` once, add yourself to the video group,
then log in on a TTY and run `omg`.
